    {
      "file": "a.mp3",
      "text": "Student A. Look carefully. Describe three details in the present. Say who or what you can see, what is happening, and one more detail. Speak slowly. Pause so your partner can remember.",
      "bytes": 198574,
      "sha256": "2f0e14de41f85b0f24d66d422ce421c65970ea70fb831f69fae791ba22ed6914"
    },
    {
      "file": "b.mp3",
      "text": "Student B. Listen to your partner. Begin with your partner’s name and said that. Report the same three ideas. Change the verbs to the past for this practice. Change I to he, she, or they when it refers to your partner. Keep the original meaning.",
      "bytes": 273807,
      "sha256": "1dad921d7e5f7da6a1eabc9f92a952c20784bdd8527d2b3527f2bb21a6732cad"
    },
    {
      "file": "guide.mp3",
      "text": "What did they say? Your teacher chooses two students. Student A describes the picture in the present. Student B reports what student A said. The class checks the meaning, the verbs and the pronouns. Then change roles for the next picture.",
      "bytes": 244132,
      "sha256": "a97e406ebb0b8885d387d64fae596ea602a4e630f13008dad83826ad53bcbfcb"
